  📗
    Has the route stand aside for other methods, and returns it. When no
    route has a request's method, the answer is a 405 that lists the methods
    of the routes that do match the path. A route that stands aside is not
    counted among them: to a method that is not its own it is not there.
    This is for a catch-all that answers whatever nothing else did, such as
    a directory of files at the root of a site, or a page to fall back on.
    Without it such a route makes a 405 of every path that has no route, for
    every method but its own, where a client should be told 404.
