  📗
    Serves the files of *files* under *path*, to GET and HEAD, and returns
    the route, which takes notes like any other. The route ends in a
    catch-all, so every route that is more specific wins over it: a file is
    only looked for when nothing else answers the path. It stands aside for
    other methods (🔇), so a POST to a path under it is answered as it would
    be without the mount. A directory that is not there is a startup
    problem.
